2026-11-09T10:46Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

git-erg ticket 0308 (PR MinhHaDuong/git-erg#394) removes the advisory
`erg check` warning `regressive log timestamps`. The spec sets no ordering
rule on the log (append-only, never edited), and the only remedy the
warning invited, reordering lines, the spec forbids; it fired on 44 files
of git-erg's own store.

tests/test_erg_log_placement.py:103-111
(`test_check_warns_on_displaced_and_regressive_fixtures`, from ticket 0879)
asserts `WARN 0002-regressive-timestamp.erg: regressive log timestamps` on
stderr of the committed tickets/erg. It goes red when this store syncs a
binary that includes #394.

## Actions

- Drop the regressive assertion and its 0002-regressive-timestamp.erg
  fixture; keep the displaced-entry assertion. Optionally assert the
  regressive fixture now draws no warning.
- Reword the module docstring that justifies "regressive" as advisory.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] the test passes against a tickets/erg that includes git-erg #394
- [ ] the displaced-entry assertion is unchanged

Not actionable until git-erg #394 merges and this store syncs its binary;
land it in the same PR as that sync.
